# Project Context

## Purpose

- Impress visitors
- Serve as a portfolio for my past coding projects
- Give visitors an idea of what I'm like as a person and as a creative
- Demonstrate my skills as a Software Engineer
- Give visitors the means to contact me

## Tech Stack

### Frontend
- React 19 + TypeScript (strict mode)
- Vite 5 for bundling
- React Router v7 for routing
- MUI (Material UI) v7 with custom dark theme (`src/theme.ts`)
- Emotion for CSS-in-JS (via MUI)
- MDX for content authoring (blog posts, project write-ups, gallery posts)
  - Remark plugins: frontmatter, GFM, TOC, mdx-frontmatter
  - Rehype plugins: slug, callouts (Obsidian theme), pretty-code (Shiki, github-dark)
- Cloudflare Turnstile for bot protection on forms

### Backend (CDK Infrastructure)
- AWS CDK v2 (TypeScript) for infrastructure-as-code
- AWS HTTP API Gateway — single API serving all backend routes
- AWS Lambda (Node.js 22.x) — serverless handlers for contact and analytics
- AWS DynamoDB — analytics event storage (90-day TTL)
- AWS SES — transactional email for contact form submissions
- AWS Secrets Manager — stores Turnstile secret key
- Zod — runtime schema validation in Lambda handlers

## Project Structure

- `infra/` — CDK infrastructure (see CDK Infrastructure section)
- `src/pages/` — Route-level page components (one per route)
- `src/components/` — Reusable UI components, organized by feature:
  - `src/components/blog/` — BlogCard, BlogLayout, Heading, mdxMapping
  - `src/components/projects/` — ProjectCard, ProjectLayout
  - `src/components/gallery/` — GalleryCard, GalleryImageList, GalleryImageStack, GalleryLayout
  - Root-level components: Hero, Navbar, SocialLinks, UnderConstruction, ScrollPhysicsImage, ViewportPerspectiveBox
- `src/lib/` — Content loaders and standalone engines:
  - `blog.ts`, `projects.ts`, `gallery.ts` — MDX content loading via `import.meta.glob`
  - `ScrollPhysicsElement.ts` — Scroll-responsive animation engine (standalone class)
- `src/hooks/` — Custom React hooks:
  - `useAnalytics.ts` — Pageview + duration tracking (HTTPS-only, used in App.tsx)
  - `useContentBySlug.ts` — Generic lazy content loader by slug
  - `useHashScroll.ts` — URL hash-based scroll navigation
  - `useScrollPhysics.ts` — Scroll animation controller (uses ScrollPhysicsElement)
- `src/types/` — TypeScript type definitions (`blog.ts`, `project.ts`, `gallery.ts`, `mdx.ts`)
- `src/content/` — MDX content files:
  - `src/content/blog/` — Blog posts
  - `src/content/projects/` — Project write-ups
  - `src/content/gallery/` — Gallery posts

## Content Architecture

All content types follow the same pattern:
1. **Types** (`src/types/`): `Frontmatter` → `Meta` (adds `slug`) → full type (adds `Content`)
2. **Loader** (`src/lib/`): `getAll*()` (eager, for listing pages) + `get*BySlug()` (lazy, for detail pages)
3. **Listing page** (`src/pages/`): Calls `getAll*()`, renders cards in a grid/stack
4. **Detail page** (`src/pages/`): Uses `useParams` + `useEffect` to lazy-load by slug, renders in a layout wrapper
5. **Components** (`src/components/<feature>/`): Card component for listings, Layout component for detail pages

MDX frontmatter is extracted via `remark-mdx-frontmatter` and typed per content type.

## Routing

| Path | Page | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `/` | Home | Hero section with animated name/subtitle videos |
| `/about` | About | ViewportPerspectiveBox + scroll-driven physics animation |
| `/blog` | Blog | Blog post listing |
| `/blog/:slug` | BlogPost | Individual blog post |
| `/projects` | Projects | Project grid |
| `/projects/:slug` | ProjectPage | Individual project write-up |
| `/gallery` | Gallery | Gallery listing with stacked image previews |
| `/gallery/:slug` | GalleryPage | Individual gallery item detail |
| `/resume` | Resume | Contact form with Turnstile CAPTCHA |
| `*` | — | Redirects to `/` |

## CDK Infrastructure (`infra/`)

- **Entry point**: `infra/bin/infra.ts`
- **Main stack**: `infra/lib/contact-api-stack.ts` — `PersonalSiteContactApi`
- **Lambda handlers**:
  - `infra/lambda/contact/index.ts` — validates form input, verifies Turnstile token, sends email via SES
  - `infra/lambda/analytics/index.ts` — validates origin, writes pageview/duration events to DynamoDB
- **API routes** (HTTP API, rate-limited to 10 req/s / burst 50):
  - `POST /contact` → ContactHandler
  - `POST /analytics` → AnalyticsHandler
- **DynamoDB table**: `PersonalSiteAnalytics` — PAY_PER_REQUEST, 90-day TTL, RETAIN removal policy
  - Partition key: `pk` (`DATE#YYYY-MM-DD`), Sort key: `sk` (`{TYPE}#{ISO_TIMESTAMP}#{UUID}`)
- **Secrets Manager**: `personal-site/turnstile-secret-key` — Turnstile API secret (read by ContactHandler)
- **CORS**: Restricted to `https://chrisbeckermitchell.com`
- **CDK context** (`infra/cdk.json`): `senderEmail`, `recipientEmail`, `allowedOrigins`
- **Scripts**: `build` (tsc), `synth` (cdk synth), `deploy` (cdk deploy), `diff` (cdk diff)

## Analytics

The `useAnalytics` hook (called once in `App.tsx`) tracks route changes:
- **pageview** event: path, referrer, sessionId, language, viewport dimensions, User-Agent
- **duration** event: path, durationMs, sessionId (sent via `sendBeacon()` on unmount)
- Bails out when `window.isSecureContext` is false (no tracking over HTTP)
- Session ID generated with `crypto.randomUUID()` and stored in `sessionStorage`
- Sends to `${VITE_CONTACT_API_URL}/analytics`

## Forms & Security

- Resume request form at `/resume` with Cloudflare Turnstile bot protection
- Test Turnstile key used in development, real key in production
- Form submission POSTs JSON to `VITE_CONTACT_API_URL/contact`

## Environment Variables

- `VITE_CONTACT_API_URL` — Base URL for the CDK-deployed API (serves both `/contact` and `/analytics`)
- `VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY` — Cloudflare Turnstile site key (test key in dev)

## Coding Preferences

- Use functional components with hooks (no class components)
- TypeScript for all new files
- Prefer named exports over default exports
- Follow existing component patterns for consistency
- Follow modern best practices whenever possible

## Key Patterns

- **Barrel exports**: Each component directory has an `index.ts` re-exporting its public API
- **MUI imports**: Use deep imports (`import Box from '@mui/material/Box'`) not named imports from the package root
- **MDX rendering**: Blog and project layouts share `mdxComponents` from `src/components/blog/mdxMapping.tsx`
- **Responsive design**: MUI breakpoints (`xs`, `sm`, `md`) for mobile/desktop switching

## Deployment

- Frontend deploys automatically on pushes to remote main using GitHub Actions.
- Backend (CDK) deploys automatically on pushes to main that touch `infra/**` via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/deploy-infra.yml`). PRs targeting main run `cdk diff` instead. Can also be deployed manually via `cdk deploy` from `infra/`.

